  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referencing the **Georgia Motor Vehicle Division (MVD) Tag Renewal portal** at **mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx**, which is operated by the **Georgia Department of Revenue (DOR)**. Here's a summary of what that site offers and related information:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\ude97 Georgia MVD \u2013 Tag Renewal Portal\n\n**Website:** [https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx](https://mvd.dor.ga.gov/tags/index.aspx)\n\nGeorgia MVD offers online applications and information regarding **tag renewals, license plates, titles, dealer registrations, and commercial vehicles.**\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udd04 Online Tag Renewal\nGeorgia residents can renew their vehicle registration online at the portal. However, if the address on your **Renewal Notice is not correct**, you should **not** renew online.\n\nIn addition, you must present your **driver's license or Georgia ID** to renew.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83e\udeaa License Plates\nAfter vehicle registration, you will receive a **license plate with a decal**, which must be **renewed each year.**\n\nGeorgia offers **hundreds of specialty plate designs** to choose from, including veterans, colleges, special interest groups, and more.\n\nA new standard-issue license plate is also available to **commemorate the 250th anniversary of the Revolutionary War**, featuring a design created by a Georgia Middle School student.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udccb Titling a Vehicle\nWhen your vehicle requires a Georgia title, you will be **unable to register your vehicle** and obtain a Georgia license plate (tag) without a Georgia title already issued in your name, or without applying for a title at the time of registration.\n\nAn owner has **seven (7) calendar days** from the purchase or transfer date, or the date they establish residency in Georgia, to title and register their vehicle. If you fail to register during this period, you will be subject to **fines** if stopped by law enforcement.\n\nGeorgia requires a **Title Ad Valorem Tax of 6.6%** (beginning 01/01/2020) to be paid at the time of titling.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udf10 Additional Ways to Renew (besides online)\n- **By Mail:** Make a check payable to your County Tax Commissioner and mail it to your county's tax office.\n- **In Person:** Payment methods typically include MasterCard, Visa, and Discover.\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Verify the Website is Official\nCall **1-800-GEORGIA** to verify that a website is an official website of the State of Georgia.\n\n---\n\nIs there something specific you'd like help with on the Georgia MVD tag portal, such as renewing a tag, finding a tag office, or ordering a specialty plate?",
